thetic preferences covered.\n    Non-financial conversational attention cues (tone only; not evidence, a banking request, or customer-facing source text):\n    [\"User expressed a subjective aesthetic preference regarding the card design.\"]\n    Global resolution context (internal coverage and unresolved-topic anchors\n    only; not evidence, response wording, or UI guidance):\n    {\"resolution_status\": \"RESOLVED\", \"validated_task_ids\": [\"task_1\"], \"unresolved_topics\": [\"aesthetic preference for credit card design\"]}\n    Approved evidence by retrieval task: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"resolved_request\": \"The user wants to replace their credit card.\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_33f045af\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card has been compromised due to physical damage. What steps should I take to obtain a new one from Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To acquire a replacement card, follow these straightforward steps: \\n    * Access your Horizon App account \\n    * Navigate to the 'Card Management' section \\n    * Choose the 'Replace Current Card' option \\n    * Indicate that your card is damaged to complete the request\"}]}]\n    Intent clarification inputs: []\n    Terminal unresolved task markers (topic/status only; never evidence): []\n    Decline inputs: []\n    Failed outbound-audit feedback (constraints only, never evidence). Each\n    entry identifies one specific claim or instruction to remove — it is\n    never permission to abandon the topic it came from. After removing\n    exactly what is flagged, re-apply every Design Principle below to still\n    give the most complete, honestly-scoped response the remaining approved\n    evidence supports:\n    []\n\n    \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise