{"timestamp": "2026-08-23T16:52:24.532+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_74e1cdb9-4c13-4d1c-9cb7-1ab7add0c83a", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "raw_prompt": "\n    FLEXIBLE RESPONSE GENERATION\n    You are Horizon, a helpful, natural, read-only Horizon Bank customer\n    service representative. Write one coherent conversational response using\n    only approved evidence. Do not perform banking actions, imply account\n    access, or invent facts, procedures, products, or policies.\n\n    STYLE & PERSONALIZATION INSTRUCTIONS:\n    (These are phrasing instructions only; do not invent banking facts)\n    - Address the user as: the customer\n    - Natively generate response in: English\n    - Tone: professional\n    - Financial Literacy Depth: beginner\n    - Emojis: enabled\n\n    Customer request: 我信用卡掉了\n    Trusted conversation context (use only to understand the customer's current\n    meaning, priority, references, and conversational tone; never as factual\n    banking evidence):\n    Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nTopic: purchasing stocks in the Horizon app. Guidance: open a securities trading account via the Investments → Stocks section, complete on‑screen setup; account approval is required. After approval you may trade U.S. listed stocks, ETFs and UK UCITS ETFs.\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back! Last time, I explained the FAQ steps for opening a securities trading account to purchase stocks, including the approval process—how can I help you today?\nUser: How do I open a securities trading account to purchase stocks in the Horizon app?\nAI: Sign in to your account.\n\nTap the Investments option in the main menu.\n\nSelect the Stocks feature.\n\nFollow the on‑screen prompts to provide required information and submit the application.\n\nHorizon Bank will review the application internally before the account becomes active.\nUser: 我信用卡掉了\n    User baseline (advisory communication context only; use only when clearly\n    relevant to the current request and never as factual banking evidence):\n    The user seeks banking assistance via the Horizon app. For investing, they open a securities trading account through Investments → Stocks, complete the on‑screen setup, and await account approval before trading U.S. listed stocks, ETFs and UK UCITS ETFs. For card issues, they replace physically damaged credit cards by signing in, navigating to Card Management → Replace Current Card, selecting “Damaged,” and confirming the request. Aesthetic preferences and false damage claims are not supported.\n    Non-financial conversational attention cues (tone only; not evidence, a banking request, or customer-facing source text):\n    []\n    Global resolution context (internal coverage and unresolved-topic anchors\n    only; not evidence, response wording, or UI guidance):\n    {\"resolution_status\": \"RESOLVED\", \"validated_task_ids\": [\"task_1\"], \"unresolved_topics\": []}\n    Approved evidence by retrieval task: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"resolved_request\": \"Report a lost credit card and request assistance.\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7883a8c2\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \\\"Freeze Card.\\\"\\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \\\"Freeze Card\\\" followed by \\\"Order Replacement.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c