rmine your credit limit, review the assigned limit and adjust as needed.\\n   * To select your own credit limit, which may be higher than the assigned limit, follow the prompts to input your preferred amount.\\n   * If you are satisfied with the assigned credit limit, simply confirm and proceed with your application.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_6a11e443\", \"content\": \"Question: What reasons caused my Horizon credit card to be issued with a S$500 credit limit?\\n\\nAnswer: - Applicants who are granted a {{faq_6a11e443_001}} credit limit typically meet all of the following conditions:\\n- Singapore citizen or permanent resident\\n- Aged {{faq_6a11e443_002}} years or older\\n- Assessed annual income below {{faq_6a11e443_003}}\\n- No existing credit card or unsecured loan with Horizon Bank\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_2b0eca91\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the criteria for qualifying for a higher credit limit on my Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, the primary cardholder of an active account is generally eligible to request a credit limit increase, with certain exceptions. Specifically, this option is not available to customers whose Horizon card currently has a credit limit of {{faq_2b0eca91_001}}, or to those who have already reached the maximum limit of {{faq_2b0eca91_002}}K, as established by Horizon.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n  