erator to ensure that your PayNow name reflects your registered account name on record. This collaborative effort guarantees that rigorous checks are in place to verify the correctness of your updated PayNow name, providing you with assurance of its accuracy.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_0ae0bb51\", \"content\": \"Question: Do I qualify for Horizon Bank’s Instant Loan offering?\\n\\nAnswer: - **For current Horizon Bank clients:**\\n  * You need to possess a Horizon credit card and have adequate unused credit limit.\\n- **For new applicants:**\\n  * Singapore citizens, permanent residents, and foreign nationals are all permitted to apply for the Instant Loan.\\n  * Every submission will be subject to Horizon Bank’s credit‑worthiness assessment.\\n\\nYou may request a credit facility provided you satisfy the following criteria:\\n- You are aged between {{faq_0ae0bb51_001}} and {{faq_0ae0bb51_002}} years.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_003}} if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_004}} if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant informati