nformation regarding how to update or change KYC documentation, profile settings, or identification verification steps.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 3, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"None of the supplied candidate parents contain information regarding how to update or change KYC documentation, profile settings for identification verification, or identity document submission procedures.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7b4f60c3\", \"content\": \"Question: What verification process does Horizon Bank use to confirm the accuracy of my PayNow name after an update?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we work in conjunction with the PayNow scheme operator to ensure that your PayNow name reflects your registered account name on record. This collaborative effort guarantees that rigorous checks are in place to verify the correctness of your updated PayNow name, providing you with assurance of its accuracy.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_730ac28e\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank safeguard its customers' electronic payment transactions, and what responsibilities do account holders have in protecting their accounts?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we adhere to the E-Payments User Protection Guidelines set forth by the Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS), which outline the roles of both financial institutions and consumers in preventing and addressing unauthorized and erroneous transactions. To ensure the security of your protected account, which includes any account with a balance exceeding {{faq_730ac28e_001}} or equivalent, capable of electronic transactions, and issued by a relevant payment service provider, please follow these best practices: \\n   - Only download the Horizon App from authorized sources and regularly update your browser and operating system.\\n   - Provide accurate contact information and opt-in to receive transaction notifications to stay informed about your account activity.\\n   - Safeguard your One-Time Passwords (OTPs) sent via the Horizon App or SMS, and secure access to your protected account.\\n   - Carefully review risk warning messages and content from Horizon Bank before proceeding with payment transactions or engaging in high-risk activities.\\n   - Verify website addresses and phone numbers through official channels to avoid potential scams.\\n   - Understand the risks associated with high-risk activities and take necessary precautions.\\n   - Promptly report any suspicious or unauthorized activity on your account, and utilize the self-service 'kill switch' feature provided by Horizon Bank to block further access.\\n   - Cooperate with Horizon Bank by providing detailed information about unauthorized transactions and filing a police report if you suspect you've been a victim of fraud or scam.\\n   For comprehensive details on the E-Payment Guidelines, please visit the MAS website at https://www.mas.gov.sg/regulation/guidelines/e-payments-user-protection-guidelines.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b557f94d\", \"content\": \"Question: Can I edit the name shown on my account after I’ve registered?\\n\\nAnswer: - Absolutely, you can change it through the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_d68c283e\", \"content\": \"Question: How will Horizon Bank protect my identity during PayNow transfers, and what information will be displayed to the sender?\\n\\nAnswer: To bolster the security of PayNow transactions, Horizon Bank will display a partial representation of the recipient's registered account name, rather than their full name or a custom nickname. This enhanced security feature is designed to prevent impersonation scams by ensuring that only verified account information is visible to the payer. By limiting the display to select characters from the recipient's registered name, Horizon Bank strikes a balance between safeguarding user privacy and providing payers with the confidence that they are transferring funds to the intended recipient. This approach effectively curtails scammers' ability to use deceptive nicknames, thereby protecting both the payer and the payee. Key benefits of this measure include: \\n   * Mitigating the risk of impersonation scams\\n   * Enhancing payer confidence in the authenticity of transfer recipients\\n   * Protecting payee privacy through partial name display\\n   * Preventing name harvesting via PayNow's lookup feature\\n   By anchoring the display to officially registered account details, Horizon Bank ensures a more secure and trustworthy transaction experience for all users.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission,