{"timestamp": "2026-08-24T05:52:05.609+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_53fff7d9-27ae-483e-9a4c-e2fd61d1a6a5", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): can i change my kyc docs?\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: can i change my kyc docs?\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Submit updated identification documents through the secure portal or visit a branch for verification\", \"policy\": \"Customers must provide valid government issued identification and proof of address for all profile updates\", \"conceptual\": \"Know Your Customer documentation ensures account security and regulatory compliance for all banking services\", \"target_commercial_product\": [\"ALL\", \"Deposit_Account\"], \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Features And Limits\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Application\", \"Branch And ATM Locator\", \"Card Logistics\", \"Eligibility\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Transaction Disputes\"], \"customer_component\": \"How can I update my KYC documentation?\", \"direct_query\": \"How can I update my KYC documentation?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Submit updated identification documents through the secure portal or visit a branch for verification\", \"policy\": \"Customers must provide valid government issued identification and proof of address for all profile updates\", \"conceptual\": \"Know Your Customer documentation ensures account security and regulatory compliance for all banking services\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_4\", \"procedural\": \"Use the digital identity service to sync personal details and allow time for system propagation\", \"policy\": \"Personal information change requests are final and cannot be revoked once they are submitted\", \"conceptual\": \"Updating identification records is necessary to maintain accurate account status and ensure regulatory compliance\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [\"faq_6e2d941d\"], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The supplied parent discusses email authenticity and Customer Care contact details, which does not provide materially relevant information for updating KYC documentation.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The supplied candidate parents discuss PayNow transaction proxy display names and missing coupon redemption troubleshooting, which provide no relevant information regarding how to update or change KYC documentation.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 3, \"status\": \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"faq_6e2d941d\"], \"reason\": \"The supplied parent faq_6e2d941d provides specific procedures for updating address details which are part of KYC documentation, but it does not address other KYC documents such as identity cards.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_29a71c6f\", \"fact\": \"Personal details can be updated via Singpass with a required wait time for changes to propagate.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_824abbaf\", \"fact\": \"Mobile phone numbers for PayNow can be unlinked and updated in the app profile settings.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_9e372c30\", \"fact\": \"Submitted personal-information change requests cannot be revoked once sent.\"}]}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7b4f60c3\", \"content\": \"Question: What verification process does Horizon Bank use to confirm the accuracy of my PayNow name after an update?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we work in conjunction with the PayNow scheme operator to ensure that your PayNow name reflects your registered account name on record. This collaborative effort guarantees that rigorous checks are in place to verify the correctness of your updated PayNow name, providing you with assurance of its accuracy.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_76c34cea\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it required to book an appointment before visiting the Horizon Experience Centre for in‑person identity verification?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you submitted a manual application before {{faq_76c34cea_001}} December {{faq_76c34cea_002}}, you may attend without scheduling an appointment.\\n- From {{faq_76c34cea_003}} December {{faq_76c34cea_004}} onward, we recommend completing the application via MyInfo authentication, which is faster and more secure. Ensure your SingPass details are current before you apply.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7fc44444\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank collaborate with regulatory bodies to combat cyber threats and protect customers from fraudulent activities?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we are committed to safeguarding our customers' interests through a collaborative approach with the Monetary Authority of Singapore and other relevant authorities. The Shared Responsibility Framework is a pivotal initiative that underscores the importance of joint efforts between banks, regulatory bodies, and customers in preventing and mitigating the impact of scams. This framework specifically addresses vulnerabilities that scammers may exploit, including impersonation of legitimate entities, such as government agencies or financial institutions like Horizon Bank, where fraudsters deceive customers into divulging sensitive information. Additionally, it tackles the risks associated with malicious links sent via digital platforms, which can lead to the compromise of account credentials. By promoting a culture of shared responsibility, we aim to empower our customers with the knowledge and best practices necessary to secure their financial information and transactions, thereby fostering a safer digital banking environment for all.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_5b37494f\", \"content\": \"Question: What should I prepare and bring when I visit a Horizon Bank Experience Centre?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you filed a paper application before {{faq_5b37494f_001}} Dec {{faq_5b37494f_002}} and did not use MyInfo, you must appear at a Horizon Bank Experience Centre for in‑person identity verification. Bring the original identification documents:\\n  • NRIC for Singapore citizens or permanent residents.\\n  • Passport for Work Pass or Dependent Pass holders.\\n- A Horizon representative will confirm your identity and continue processing your request.\\n- You can monitor the application’s progress through the Horizon App.\\n- From {{faq_5b37494f_003}} Dec {{faq_5b37494f_004}} onward, we advise using MyInfo authentication for a faster, more secure submission. Ensure your SingPass details are up‑to‑date before applying.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_6e2d941d\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for changing my home address when applying for a Horizon Bank account?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Singapore citizens and Permanent Residents (effective {{faq_6e2d941d_001}} Oct {{faq_6e2d941d_002}})**: All address modifications must be submitted through Singpass. Steps:\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_003}}. Sign in to Singpass and choose your language.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_004}}. Verify that the details entered in your Horizon Bank application are accurate before proceeding.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_005}}. Submit the request; ICA will mail a {{faq_6e2d941d_006}}‑digit PIN to your new residence.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_007}}. For local addresses, the PIN letter typically arrives within one week.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_008}}. Use the PIN to continue your Horizon Bank onboarding via the ICA e‑Service portal. (Further guidance available via the provided link.)\\n- **Non‑Singapore residents**:\\n  - *Option {{faq_6e2d941d_009}}*: Access the myTax Portal with your Singpass or Singpass Foreign Account (SFA), select “Update Contact Details,” and amend your residential or mailing address. The update is reflected within three business days. (More information at the linked page.)\\n  - *Option {{faq_6e2d941d_010}}*: Go to the Ministry of Manpower (MoM) website and follow these actions:\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_011}}. Click “Log in for EP Online with Singpass” under the pass‑holder section.\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_012}}. Log in using your Singpass credentials.\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_013}}. Choose “Change Particulars – Personal Contact Details and Residential Address of Pass Holder.”\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_014}}. Input your Main Pass ID and search.\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_015}}. Edit the residential postal address and save the changes.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader concl