ntation?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Submit updated identification documents through the secure portal or visit a branch for verification\", \"policy\": \"Customers must provide valid government issued identification and proof of address for all profile updates\", \"conceptual\": \"Know Your Customer documentation ensures account security and regulatory compliance for all banking services\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The supplied parent discusses email authenticity and Customer Care contact details, which provides no materially relevant facts for updating KYC documentation.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The candidate parents discuss PayNow proxy name masking and coupon redemption issues via Customer Care chat, which provide no materially relevant facts or guidance for updating KYC documentation.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_29a71c6f\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps should I take if the data pulled from MyInfo is incorrect?\\n\\nAnswer: - Update your personal details via Singpass.\\n- Wait between {{faq_29a71c6f_001}} and {{faq_29a71c6f_002}} hours for the changes to propagate before re‑submitting your request.\\n- Verify that the address listed in MyInfo is a Singapore address.\\n- Note that for Singapore citizens and permanent residents, address updates may require additional time to appear in MyInfo.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_6e2d941d\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for changing my home address when applying for a Horizon Bank account?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Singapore citizens and Permanent Residents (effective {{faq_6e2d941d_001}} Oct {{faq_6e2d941d_002}})**: All address modifications must be submitted through Singpass. Steps:\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_003}}. Sign in to Singpass and choose your language.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_004}}. Verify that the details entered in your Horizon Bank application are accurate before proceeding.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_005}}. Submit the request; ICA will mail a {{faq_6e2d941d_006}}‑digit PIN to your new residence.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_007}}. For local addresses, the PIN letter typically arrives within one week.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_008}}. Use the PIN to continue your Horizon Bank onboarding via the ICA e‑Service portal. (Further guidance available via the provided link.)\\n- **Non‑Singapore residents**:\\n  - *Option {{faq_6e2d941d_009}}*: Access the myTax Portal with your Singpass or Singpass Foreign Account (SFA), select “Update Contact Details,” and amend your residential or mailing address. The update is reflected within three business days. (More information at the linked page.)\\n  - *Option {{faq_6e2d941d_010}}*: Go to the Ministry of Manpower (MoM) website and follow these actions:\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_011}}. Click “Log in for EP Online with Singpass” under the pass‑holder section.\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_012}}. Log in using your Singpass credentials.\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_013}}. Choose “Change Particulars – Personal Contact Details and Residential Address of Pass Holder.”\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_014}}. Input your Main Pass ID and search.\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_015}}. Edit the residential postal address and save the changes.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_824abbaf\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps do I need to follow to change my mobile phone number after it has been linked to my Horizon Savings Account for PayNow?\\n\\nAnswer: - Updating your mobile number for PayNow can be done in three straightforward actions:\\n{{faq_824abbaf_001}}. Unlink the existing phone number from PayNow through the Horizon App.\\n{{faq_824abbaf_002}}. Enter and save your new mobile number in the app’s profile settings.\\n{{faq_824abbaf_003}}. Re‑enroll the new number for PayNow by associating it with your Horizon Savings Account.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_9e372c30\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it possible to withdraw a submitted personal‑information change request?\\n\\nAnswer: - Once an update request has been sent, it cannot be revoked. If you need to modify the information, you may file a new request: for phone number or email changes, wait {{faq_9e372c30_001}} hours before submitting again; address changes can be re‑submitted immediately.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PART