ntation?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Submit updated identification documents through the secure portal or visit a branch for verification\", \"policy\": \"Customers must provide valid government issued identification and proof of address for all profile updates\", \"conceptual\": \"Know Your Customer documentation ensures account security and regulatory compliance for all banking services\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_4\", \"procedural\": \"Log in to the secure portal to upload new identification documents for manual review by staff\", \"policy\": \"Updated personal information requires a mandatory processing period before further changes can be submitted online\", \"conceptual\": \"Regulatory standards require periodic verification of customer identity documents to maintain active and compliant banking accounts\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [\"faq_29a71c6f\", \"faq_6e2d941d\"], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The supplied parent discusses email authenticity and Customer Care contact details, which provides no materially relevant facts for updating KYC documentation.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The candidate parents discuss PayNow proxy name masking and coupon redemption issues via Customer Care chat, which provide no materially relevant facts or guidance for updating KYC documentation.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 3, \"status\": \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"faq_29a71c6f\", \"faq_6e2d941d\"], \"reason\": \"The candidate parents provide useful, grounded procedures for updating specific personal details and address information via Singpass and MyInfo, but do not provide general instructions for updating all types of KYC documentation.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_824abbaf\", \"fact\": \"Mobile phone numbers linked to a Horizon Savings Account for PayNow can be updated by unlinking the existing number, entering the new number in app profile settings, and re-enrolling it.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_9e372c30\", \"fact\": \"Submitted personal-information change requests cannot be revoked once sent, and phone number or email changes require waiting {{faq_9e372c30_001}} hours before submitting a new request while address changes can be re-submitted immediately.\"}]}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7b4f60c3\", \"content\": \"Question: What verification process does Horizon Bank use to confirm the accuracy of my PayNow name after an update?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we work in conjunction with the PayNow scheme operator to ensure that your PayNow name reflects your registered account name on record. This collaborative effort guarantees that rigorous checks are in place to verify the correctness of your updated PayNow name, providing you with assurance of its accuracy.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7fc44444\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank collaborate with regulatory bodies to combat cyber threats and protect customers from fraudulent activities?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we are committed to safeguarding our customers' interests through a collaborative approach with the Monetary Authority of Singapore and other relevant authorities. The Shared Responsibility Framework is a pivotal initiative that underscores the importance of joint efforts between banks, regulatory bodies, and customers in preventing and mitigating the impact of scams. This framework specifically addresses vulnerabilities that scammers may exploit, including impersonation of legitimate entities, such as government agencies or financial institutions like Horizon Bank, where fraudsters deceive customers into divulging sensitive information. Additionally, it tackles the risks associated with malicious links sent via digital platforms, which can lead to the compromise of account credentials. By promoting a culture of shared responsibility, we aim to empower our customers with the knowledge and best practices necessary to secure their financial information and transactions, thereby fostering a safer digital banking environment for all.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_76c34cea\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it required to book an appointment before visiting the Horizon Experience Centre for in‑person identity verification?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you submitted a manual application before {{faq_76c34cea_001}} December {{faq_76c34cea_002}}, you may attend without scheduling an appointment.\\n- From {{faq_76c34cea_003}} December {{faq_76c34cea_004}} onward, we recommend completing the application via MyInfo authentication, which is faster and more secure. Ensure your SingPass details are current before you apply.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_730ac28e\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank safeguard its customers' electronic payment transactions, and what responsibilities do account holders have in protecting their accounts?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we adhere to the E-Payments User Protection Guidelines set forth by the Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS), which outline the roles of both financial institutions and consumers in preventing and addressing unauthorized and erroneous transactions. To ensure the security of your protected account, which includes any account with a balance exceeding {{faq_730ac28e_001}} or equivalent, capable of electronic transactions, and issued by a relevant payment service provider, please follow these best practices: \\n   - Only download the Horizon App from authorized sources and regularly update your browser and operating system.\\n   - Provide accurate contact information and opt-in to receive transaction notifications to stay informed about your account activity.\\n   - Safeguard your One-Time Passwords (OTPs) sent via the Horizon App or SMS, and secure access to your protected account.\\n   - Carefully review risk warning messages and content from Horizon Bank before proceeding with payment transactions or engaging in high-risk activities.\\n   - Verify website addresses and phone numbers through official channels to avoid potential scams.\\n   - Understand the risks associated with high-risk activities and take necessary precautions.\\n   - Promptly report any suspicious or unauthorized activity on your account, and utilize the self-service 'kill switch' feature provided by Horizon Bank to block further access.\\n   - Cooperate with Horizon Bank by providing detailed information about unauthorized transactions and filing a police report if you suspect you've been a victim of fraud or scam.\\n   For comprehensive details on the E-Payment Guidelines, please visit the MAS website at https://www.mas.gov.sg/regulation/guidelines/e-payments-user-protection-guidelines.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_29a71c6f\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps should I take if the data pulled from MyInfo is incorrect?\\n\\nAnswer: - Update your personal details via Singpass.\\n- Wait between {{faq_29a71c6f_001}} and {{faq_29a71c6f_002}} hours for the changes to propagate before re‑submitting your request.\\n- Verify that the address listed in MyInfo is a Singapore address.\\n- Note that for Singapore citizens and permanent residents, address updates may require additional time to appear in MyInfo.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_6e2d941d\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for changing my home address when applying for a Horizon Bank account?\\n\\nAnswer: - **Singapore citizens and Permanent Residents (effective {{faq_6e2d941d_001}} Oct {{faq_6e2d941d_002}})**: All address modifications must be submitted through Singpass. Steps:\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_003}}. Sign in to Singpass and choose your language.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_004}}. Verify that the details entered in your Horizon Bank application are accurate before proceeding.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_005}}. Submit the request; ICA will mail a {{faq_6e2d941d_006}}‑digit PIN to your new residence.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_007}}. For local addresses, the PIN letter typically arrives within one week.\\n  {{faq_6e2d941d_008}}. Use the PIN to continue your Horizon Bank onboarding via the ICA e‑Service portal. (Further guidance available via the provided link.)\\n- **Non‑Singapore residents**:\\n  - *Option {{faq_6e2d941d_009}}*: Access the myTax Portal with your Singpass or Singpass Foreign Account (SFA), select “Update Contact Details,” and amend your residential or mailing address. The update is reflected within three business days. (More information at the linked page.)\\n  - *Option {{faq_6e2d941d_010}}*: Go to the Ministry of Manpower (MoM) website and follow these actions:\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_011}}. Click “Log in for EP Online with Singpass” under the pass‑holder section.\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_012}}. Log in using your Singpass credentials.\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_013}}. Choose “Change Particulars – Personal Contact Details and Residential Address of Pass Holder.”\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_014}}. Input your Main Pass ID and search.\\n    {{faq_6e2d941d_015}}. Edit the residential postal address and save the changes.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT