ntation?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Submit updated identification documents through the secure portal or visit a branch for verification\", \"policy\": \"Customers must provide valid government issued identification and proof of address for all profile updates\", \"conceptual\": \"Know Your Customer documentation ensures account security and regulatory compliance for all banking services\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_4\", \"procedural\": \"Use the digital identity portal to sync your latest personal information with bank records automatically\", \"policy\": \"Changes to personal identification details require a mandatory processing period before they become active for use\", \"conceptual\": \"Updating regulatory documentation ensures that your account remains compliant with current financial security and identity standards\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The candidate parent discusses email security and phishing verification steps, which is irrelevant to updating KYC documentation.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The candidate parents discuss PayNow proxy name masking and coupon redemption issues, which are entirely unrelated to updating KYC documentation.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 3, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The candidate parents discuss updating personal details via Singpass, changing home addresses, updating mobile numbers for PayNow, and withdrawing personal-information change requests, but none of them address how to update or change general KYC documentation.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_29a71c6f\", \"fact\": \"Personal details can be updated via Singpass with a wait time between {{faq_29a71c6f_001}} and {{faq_29a71c6f_002}} hours for changes to propagate.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_6e2d941d\", \"fact\": \"Home address changes for Singapore citizens and permanent residents must be submitted through Singpass.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_824abbaf\", \"fact\": \"Mobile phone numbers linked to Horizon Savings Account for PayNow can be changed by unlinking the existing number, entering the new number in the app settings, and re-enrolling it.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_9e372c30\", \"fact\": \"Submitted personal-information change requests cannot be revoked once sent, but a new request can be filed.\"}]}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7fc44444\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank collaborate with regulatory bodies to combat cyber threats and protect customers from fraudulent activities?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we are committed to safeguarding our customers' interests through a collaborative approach with the Monetary Authority of Singapore and other relevant authorities. The Shared Responsibility Framework is a pivotal initiative that underscores the importance of joint efforts between banks, regulatory bodies, and customers in preventing and mitigating the impact of scams. This framework specifically addresses vulnerabilities that scammers may exploit, including impersonation of legitimate entities, such as government agencies or financial institutions like Horizon Bank, where fraudsters deceive customers into divulging sensitive information. Additionally, it tackles the risks associated with malicious links sent via digital platforms, which can lead to the compromise of account credentials. By promoting a culture of shared responsibility, we aim to empower our customers with the knowledge and best practices necessary to secure their financial information and transactions, thereby fostering a safer digital banking environment for all.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7b4f60c3\", \"content\": \"Question: What verification process does Horizon Bank use to confirm the accuracy of my PayNow name after an update?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we work in conjunction with the PayNow scheme operator to ensure that your PayNow name reflects your registered account name on record. This collaborative effort guarantees that rigorous checks are in place to verify the correctness of your updated PayNow name, providing you with assurance of its accuracy.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_5b37494f\", \"content\": \"Question: What should I prepare and bring when I visit a Horizon Bank Experience Centre?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you filed a paper application before {{faq_5b37494f_001}} Dec {{faq_5b37494f_002}} and did not use MyInfo, you must appear at a Horizon Bank Experience Centre for in‑person identity verification. Bring the original identification documents:\\n  • NRIC for Singapore citizens or permanent residents.\\n  • Passport for Work Pass or Dependent Pass holders.\\n- A Horizon representative will confirm your identity and continue processing your request.\\n- You can monitor the application’s progress through the Horizon App.\\n- From {{faq_5b37494f_003}} Dec {{faq_5b37494f_004}} onward, we advise using MyInfo authentication for a faster, more secure submission. Ensure your SingPass details are up‑to‑date before applying.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_76c34cea\", \"content\": \"Question: Is it required to book an appointment before visiting the Horizon Experience Centre for in‑person identity verification?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you submitted a manual application before {{faq_76c34cea_001}} December {{faq_76c34cea_002}}, you may attend without scheduling an appointment.\\n- From {{faq_76c34cea_003}} December {{faq_76c34cea_004}} onward, we recommend completing the application via MyInfo authentication, which is faster and more secure. Ensure your SingPass details are current before you apply.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundar