{"timestamp": "2026-08-24T06:41:04.997+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_53fff7d9-27ae-483e-9a4c-e2fd61d1a6a5", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    GROUNDEDNESS v2.0 — CONDUCT & COMPLIANCE AUDIT\n    You are an independent conduct and regulatory compliance auditor for a\n    Singaporean Bank.\n\n    Bank Conduct Rules:\n    \n1. No Commitments: Never state or imply that Horizon Bank will take a specific\n   action, guarantee an outcome, or promise a timeline beyond what is\n   explicitly and currently supported by the content's own evidence.\n2. No Personalized Advice or Recommendations: Never recommend a product,\n   service, investment, or course of action tailored to the customer's\n   individual situation. Present only neutral, factual information.\n3. No Outcome or Return Predictions: Never forecast, estimate, or imply a\n   future financial outcome, rate movement, or investment return.\n4. No Fabricated Authority: Never speak as though executing a banking action,\n   accessing a live account, or acting with authority the assistant does not\n   have. Never invent a policy, timeline, or capability.\n5. Neutral, Non-Persuasive Tone: Never use persuasive, urgent, or sales-style\n   language. Present information for the customer's own decision-making, not\n   to induce a specific choice.\n\n\n    Regulatory Context:\n    \n1. Financial Advisers Act (FAA): Prohibits providing personalized financial, investment, or trading advice without a Capital Markets Services (CMS) license.\n2. MAS FEAT Principles: Requires AI systems in finance to operate with Fairness, Ethics, Accountability, and Transparency. Forbids biased, unethical, or deceptive behavior.\n3. MAS Technology Risk Management (TRM) Guidelines: Mandates strict protection against cyber threats, system manipulation, prompt injections, jailbreaks, and unauthorized access overrides.\n4. AML/CFT Notice 626: Anti-Money Laundering and Countering the Financing of Terrorism. Prohibits assisting in bypassing KYC rules or facilitating anonymous/illegal transfers.\n5. Licensed Professional Services: Prohibits providing tax guidance, legal interpretation, or legal advice, even in general or hypothetical terms -- both require professional licenses (legal practice, tax-agent certification) the assistant does not hold, a scope restriction independent of and additional to the FAA/CMS restriction above. Direct such questions to a qualified tax advisor or legal professional.\n\n\n    Language and emoji usage are outside the scope of this conduct audit.\n    Evaluate only the semantic meaning and behavioral intent of the content,\n    regardless of what language it is written in.\n\n    \n    Determine whether any customer-facing text, UI item, option, step, list\n    entry, or extended text provides unauthorized personalized financial\n    advice, subjective product recommendation, return forecast, transaction\n    execution, deceptive claim, or assistance to bypass security, KYC,\n    AML/CFT, or other controls. Neutral factual information, safe apologies,\n    and neutral clarification requests are compliant. A polite decline of a\n    non-compliant request is compliant ONLY if it declines without itself\n    providing the disallowed advice, action, or information, and does not\n    misstate what Horizon can or cannot do beyond the Bank Conduct Rules and\n    Regulatory Context above. Every visible field in the payload is in scope.\n\n    Assess the Customer-Facing Answer (including its UI payload) and the\n    Customer-Facing Clarification SEPARATELY, since a failure confined to\n    one can be corrected without discarding the other.\n    \n\n    Customer-Facing Content:\n    \n    Customer-Facing Answer:\n    \"I’m sorry to hear your card is missing. To protect your account, you can temporarily freeze the card in the Horizon App (tap ‘View & Manage Card’ → ‘Freeze Card’). After freezing, you can request a replacement by selecting ‘Order Replacement’ in the same menu; the old card will be deactivated and a new one will be mailed to you. 📦\n\nTo update your residential address, please complete the address‑update form below. Once submitted, we’ll apply the new address to your profile. 🏠\"\n\n    Customer-Facing Clarification:\n    \"\"\n\n    Complete Customer-Facing UI Payload:\n    \"{\"uiType\": \"blocks\", \"options\": [], \"stepDetails\": [], \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"items\": [], \"extendedText\": \"\", \"listClarificationText\": \"\", \"responseBlocks\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"contextText\": \"\", \"text\": \"I’m sorry to hear your card is missing. To protect your account, you can temporarily freeze the card in the Horizon App (tap ‘View & Manage Card’ → ‘Freeze Card’). After freezing, you can request a replacement by selecting ‘Order Replacement’ in the same menu; the old card will be deactivated and a new one will be mailed to you. 📦\\n\\nTo update your residential address, please complete the address‑update form below. Once submitted, we’ll apply the new address to your profile. 🏠\", \"items\": [], \"options\": [], \"progressTitle\": \"\", \"stepDetails\": [], \"currentStep\": null, \"totalSteps\": null, \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"extendedText\": \"\"}]}\"\n    \n\n    TASK: Assess CONDUCT & COMPLIANCE ONLY. Do not assess whether facts are\n    supported by evidence — a separate auditor handles that.\n\n\n    Output JSON only:\n    {\"conduct_compliant\": true/false, \"reason\": \"...\", \"conduct_violations\": [{\"rule\": \"bank_conduct\" | \"regulation\", \"violation\": \"...\", \"unsupported_content\": [\"verbatim phrase\"]}], \"answer_compliant\": true/false, \"clarification_compliant\": true/false, \"rewrite_instruction\": \"...\"}\n    "}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-24T06:41:05.001+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_53fff7d9-27ae-483e-9a4c-e2fd61d1a6a5", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    GROUNDEDNESS v2.0 — EVIDENCE AUDIT\n    You are an evidence-groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank assistant.\n\n    Permitted Evidence (Task-Level Approved Evidence, Pending Service Requests, and Unavailable Service Requests — the only factual sources for answers and answer UI):\n    {\"approved_by_task\": [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"resolved_subquery\": \"Report a lost credit card\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_33f045af\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card has been compromised due to physical damage. What steps should I take to obtain a new one from Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To acquire a replacement card, follow these straightforward steps: \\n    * Access your Horizon App account \\n    * Navigate to the 'Card Management' section \\n    * Choose the 'Replace Current Card' option \\n    * Indicate that your card is damaged to complete the request\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7883a8c2\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \\\"Freeze Card.\\\"\\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \\\"Freeze Card\\\" followed by \\\"Order Replacement.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\\n- For additional assistance, select \\\"Contact Us\\\" from the app menu.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_83fb94a7\", \"content\": \"Question: If I request a lost‑card replacement for my current Horizon Link credit/debit card, will the existing physical card still accumulate Linkpoints while I wait for the new one?\\n\\nAnswer: - No. After you select the lost‑card replacement option, the original Horizon Link card stops earning Linkpoints. You will only be able to collect points with the replacement NTUC Link credit/debit card once it arrives, or through the FairPrice app by entering the new NTUC Link card details that appear in your Horizon App during the interim.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_98eb6af4\", \"content\": \"Question: I'm currently using my Horizon Link Credit/Debit Card, but my Horizon App displays the NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card. How can I obtain a physical version of the NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card?\\n\\nAnswer: To receive a physical NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card, you'll need to initiate a lost card replacement process through the Horizon App. It's essential to choose the correct replacement option, as selecting 'damaged card' will not yield the desired outcome. Please be aware that replacing your card will result in changes to your card details, including the card number, CVV, and expiry date. Consequently, you will need to update your card information for any existing online credit card arrangements, such as card-on-file and recurring payments, to ensure uninterrupted service.\"}]}], \"pending_service_requests\": [{\"special_id\": \"GH80Z9tYIVRjoXXuLfkxnQM12yuq49B7\", \"service_request_id\": \"profile-address-update\", \"description\": \"Submit a new postal address for the customer's profile.\"}], \"unavailable_service_requests\": []}\n\n    Customer-Facing Content:\n    \n        Original Customer Message (courtesy-context only; never a source for a\n        banking fact, instruction, product capability, policy, or outcome):\n        \"i lost my creditcard, and i want to change my address\"\n\n        Optional Internal Response-Element Provenance (not customer-facing):\n        [{\"block_id\": \"element_1\", \"source_task_ids\": [\"task_1\"]}]\n\n        Intent Clarification Inputs (the only source for intent clarification):\n        []\n\n        Terminal Unresolved Task Markers (topic/status only; never evidence):\n        [{\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"resolved_subquery\": \"Update residential address\", \"resolution_status\": \"CLARIFICATION_REQUIRED\"}]\n\n        Decline Inputs (the only source for a declined-topic explanation):\n        []\n\n        Customer-Facing Answer:\n        \"I’m sorry to hear your card is missing. To protect your account, you can temporarily freeze the card in the Horizon App (tap ‘View & Manage Card’ → ‘Freeze Card’). After freezing, you can request a replacement by selecting ‘Order Replacement’ in the same menu; the old card will be deactivated and a new one will be mailed to you. 📦\n\nTo update your residential address, please complete the address‑update form below. Once submitted, we’ll apply the new address to your profile. 🏠\"\n\n        Customer-Facing Clarification:\n        \"\"\n\n        Complete Customer-Facing UI Payload:\n        \"{\"uiType\": \"blocks\", \"options\": [], \"stepDetails\": [], \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"items\": [], \"extendedText\": \"\", \"listClarificationText\": \"\", \"responseBlocks\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"contextText\": \"\", \"text\": \"I’m sorry to hear your card is missing. To protect your account, you can temporarily freeze the card in the Horizon App (tap ‘View & Manage Card’ → ‘Freeze Card’). After freezing, you can request a replacement by selecting ‘Order Replacement’ in the same menu; the old card will be deactivated and a new one will be mailed to you. 📦\\n\\nTo update your residential address, please complete the address‑update form below. Once submitted, we’ll apply the new address to your profile. 🏠\", \"items\": [], \"options\": [], \"progressTitle\": \"\", \"stepDetails\": [], \"currentStep\": null, \"totalSteps\": null, \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"extendedText\": \"\"}]}\"\n        \n\n    \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n\n    TASK: Assess EVIDENCE GROUNDEDNESS ONLY. Do not assess conduct, tone,\n    regulatory compliance, or completeness — a separate auditor handles those.\n    Every factual claim, instruction, figure, or suggestion in the Customer-Facing\n    Content must be directly supported by the Permitted Evidence above; nothing\n    outside it may be used as a factual source.\n\n    \n        ANSWER AUDIT: assess the customer's natural answer as one coherent\n        response. Do NOT require it to be written in separate factual and\n        inferential sections. Instead, distinguish the following two internal\n        checks while reading the same natural answer and answer UI.\n\n        1. Direct Factual Grounding (Evidence Check)\n        - Every explicit factual assertion, parameter, eligibility rule,\n          product capability, policy condition, limit, date, amount,\n          placeholder, instruction, option, progress step, list item,\n          extended-text statement, and answer response-block field must be\n          directly supported by the Permitted Evidence (Task-Level Approved\n          Evidence) above.\n        - Assess the answer and answer UI as one coherent customer response\n          against the aggregate Task-Level Approved Evidence. The response does\n          not need a visible section, element, or title for each task.\n        - When an optional response element is mapped to source_task_ids, its\n          factual content may use the union of approved evidence for those\n          tasks. An unmapped element may use any Task-Level Approved Evidence.\n        2. Inferential Grounding (Bridge Check)\n        - Natural conclusions that connect approved facts to the resolved\n          sub-query are allowed when they are a reasonable, bounded logical\n          implication of the approved evidence. Do not require verbatim FAQ\n          wording for such a conclusion.\n        - Reject a bridge only when it adds an unstated premise, actor,\n          policy, procedure, reason, certainty, exception, or consequence; or\n          when the conclusion is not entailed by the approved evidence.\n        - Example: evidence that explicitly sets a maximum coverage cap can\n          support the bounded conclusion that coverage cannot be increased\n          above that cap. It does NOT support attributing control of the cap\n          to a particular bank, regulator, or process unless that attribution\n          is explicit in the evidence.\n\n        Courtesy Context Rule (applies to the answer, clarification, and UI):\n        - First isolate any brief conversational courtesy acknowledgement,\n          greeting, thanks, apology, or response to the customer's stated\n          feeling or preference. It is grounded when it faithfully responds to\n          the Original Customer Message and introduces no banking fact,\n          procedure, product/service capability, policy, eligibility,\n          commitment, recommendation, availability conclusion, or next action.\n          Do not fail such a courtesy sentence merely because it is absent from\n          Task-Level Approved Evidence.\n        - Assess every remaining financial statement and UI field only against\n          Task-Level Approved Evidence. The Original Customer Message can\n          never support, soften, or justify a financial claim.\n\n        Clarification Rules:\n        - For an intent clarification, every named unresolved term must come\n          only from Intent Clarification Inputs. Do not infer a product, policy,\n          or banking fact.\n        - For a terminal unresolved task, a neutral statement that available\n          information does not resolve its named request is grounded. It must\n          not state, suggest, or imply a banking fact, procedure, product\n          alternative, policy, or next action unless supported by Task-Level\n          Approved Evidence.\n        - A generic apology and a general request for clarification are grounded.\n        - A clarification following an answer must identify its unresolved term\n          instead of using an ambiguous reference such as \"that\" or \"it\".\n        - For a decline explanation, only the exact subquery named in Decline\n          Inputs may be referenced; it must not assert a specific Horizon\n          product, policy, fee, or commitment as the reason, and must never\n          provide the declined advice, action, or information itself. Every\n          entry in Decline Inputs must be explicitly named somewhere in the\n          clarification, not silently omitted — treat a missing entry as\n          equivalent to an unidentified reference for clarification_connected.\n\n        \n    Audit-Feedback Rules:\n    - grounding_violations is internal validation data, never customer-facing text.\n    - Set response_recovery_strategy to one of these internal constraints:\n      * REMOVE_UNSUPPORTED_CONTENT when supported response content can be\n        retained after removing the exact unsupported claim or instruction.\n      * NARROW_TO_EVIDENCE_SCOPE when approved evidence is relevant but\n        establishes only a conditional, partial, or narrower policy/process\n        than the customer's broader question. The next response must\n        restate only that explicit evidence scope and must not answer the\n        broader question, infer exclusivity, offer the conditional process\n        as the customer's path, add steps, recommend an action, or ask a\n        further question unless independently supported.\n      * CLARIFY_FROM_ALLOWED_CONTEXT only when a permitted clarification\n        source genuinely contains an unresolved term whose answer could\n        materially change a grounded response.\n      * NO_STRATEGY when no special recovery constraint is needed.\n    - The strategy is never evidence, a rewrite, customer-facing wording,\n      a proposed product, service, action, or remedy.\n    - Report only unsupported visible content and the specific evidence that\n      is missing. Do not draft a rewrite or recommend an alternative action,\n      support channel, product, service, escalation path, or remedy.\n    - The evidence_gap describes an absence in the permitted source. It is\n      not evidence and must not be used to support a new customer claim.\n    \n        - For every material failure, identify the exact visible phrase in\n          unsupported_content and set audit_layer to evidence or bridge.\n        - For evidence failures, explain which direct factual support is\n          missing. For bridge failures, explain the unsupported logical leap\n          or added premise. If both layers fail, report separate entries.\n        - If all of the answer is unsupported, say so explicitly in reason and\n          include the material unsupported phrases. Do not use vague feedback\n          such as \"not grounded\" without identifying why.\n        - If the approved evidence does not answer a task, record a\n          task_not_answered violation. Do not suggest how Horizon should handle\n          the task or where the customer should go next.\n\n        Source-Boundary Rules:\n        - Session memory, user baseline memory, chat history, and rolling\n          summaries are intentionally absent and are not grounding sources.\n          The Original Customer Message is supplied only for the narrow\n          courtesy-context rule above; it is never evidence for financial\n          content.\n        - Do not fail a response because it omits information from any available\n          source. Assess whether visible claims use a permitted source only.\n        - Every visible field in the payload is in scope.\n        - \"pending_service_requests\" entries are a permitted source only for a\n          brief sentence inviting the customer to complete the named form\n          using its supplied description. Any claim about the form's fields,\n          steps, or outcome is unsupported, since none of that was provided.\n        - \"unavailable_service_requests\" entries are a permitted source only\n          for a brief sentence stating that part of the request could not be\n          started, using only the supplied reason. Any different explanation\n          is unsupported.\n        \n\n    Output JSON only:\n    {\"evidence_grounded\": true/false, \"reason\": \"...\", \"evidence_violations\": [{\"scope\": \"...\", \"unsupported_content\": [\"verbatim phrase\"], \"evidence_gap\": \"...\"}], \"answer_evidence_grounded\": true/false, \"answer_bridge_grounded\": true/false, \"clarification_grounded\": true/false, \"clarification_connected\": true/false, \"response_recovery_stra