{"timestamp": "2026-08-24T06:41:08.478+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_53fff7d9-27ae-483e-9a4c-e2fd61d1a6a5", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    GROUNDEDNESS v2.0 — CONDUCT & COMPLIANCE AUDIT\n    You are an independent conduct and regulatory compliance auditor for a\n    Singaporean Bank.\n\n    Bank Conduct Rules:\n    \n1. No Commitments: Never state or imply that Horizon Bank will take a specific\n   action, guarantee an outcome, or promise a timeline beyond what is\n   explicitly and currently supported by the content's own evidence.\n2. No Personalized Advice or Recommendations: Never recommend a product,\n   service, investment, or course of action tailored to the customer's\n   individual situation. Present only neutral, factual information.\n3. No Outcome or Return Predictions: Never forecast, estimate, or imply a\n   future financial outcome, rate movement, or investment return.\n4. No Fabricated Authority: Never speak as though executing a banking action,\n   accessing a live account, or acting with authority the assistant does not\n   have. Never invent a policy, timeline, or capability.\n5. Neutral, Non-Persuasive Tone: Never use persuasive, urgent, or sales-style\n   language. Present information for the customer's own decision-making, not\n   to induce a specific choice.\n\n\n    Regulatory Context:\n    \n1. Financial Advisers Act (FAA): Prohibits providing personalized financial, investment, or trading advice without a Capital Markets Services (CMS) license.\n2. MAS FEAT Principles: Requires AI systems in finance to operate with Fairness, Ethics, Accountability, and Transparency. Forbids biased, unethical, or deceptive behavior.\n3. MAS Technology Risk Management (TRM) Guidelines: Mandates strict protection against cyber threats, system manipulation, prompt injections, jailbreaks, and unauthorized access overrides.\n4. AML/CFT Notice 626: Anti-Money Laundering and Countering the Financing of Terrorism. Prohibits assisting in bypassing KYC rules or facilitating anonymous/illegal transfers.\n5. Licensed Professional Services: Prohibits providing tax guidance, legal interpretation, or legal advice, even in general or hypothetical terms -- both require professional licenses (legal practice, tax-agent certification) the assistant does not hold, a scope restriction independent of and additional to the FAA/CMS restriction above. Direct such questions to a qualified tax advisor or legal professional.\n\n\n    Language and emoji usage are outside the scope of this conduct audit.\n    Evaluate only the semantic meaning and behavioral intent of the content,\n    regardless of what language it is written in.\n\n    \n    Determine whether any customer-facing text, UI item, option, step, list\n    entry, or extended text provides unauthorized personalized financial\n    advice, subjective product recommendation, return forecast, transaction\n    execution, deceptive claim, or assistance to bypass security, KYC,\n    AML/CFT, or other controls. Neutral factual information, safe apologies,\n    and neutral clarification requests are compliant. A polite decline of a\n    non-compliant request is compliant ONLY if it declines without itself\n    providing the disallowed advice, action, or information, and does not\n    misstate what Horizon can or cannot do beyond the Bank Conduct Rules and\n    Regulatory Context above. Every visible field in the payload is in scope.\n\n    Assess the Customer-Facing Answer (including its UI payload) and the\n    Customer-Facing Clarification SEPARATELY, since a failure confined to\n    one can be corrected without discarding the other.\n    \n\n    Customer-Facing Content:\n    \n    Customer-Facing Answer:\n    \"Sorry, I don't have a complete answer for the part about Report a lost credit card right now.\"\n\n    Customer-Facing Clarification:\n    \"\"\n\n    Complete Customer-Facing UI Payload:\n    \"{\"uiType\": \"blocks\", \"options\": [], \"stepDetails\": [], \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"items\": [], \"extendedText\": \"\", \"listClarificationText\": \"\", \"responseBlocks\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"contextText\": \"\", \"text\": \"Sorry, I don't have a complete answer for the part about Report a lost credit card right now.\", \"items\": [], \"options\": [], \"progressTitle\": \"\", \"stepDetails\": [], \"currentStep\": null, \"totalSteps\": null, \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"extendedText\": \"\"}]}\"\n    \n\n    TASK: Assess CONDUCT & COMPLIANCE ONLY. Do not assess whether facts are\n    supported by evidence — a separate auditor handles that.\n\n\n    Output JSON only:\n    {\"conduct_compliant\": true/false, \"reason\": \"...\", \"conduct_violations\": [{\"rule\": \"bank_conduct\" | \"regulation\", \"violation\": \"...\", \"unsupported_content\": [\"verbatim phrase\"]}], \"answer_compliant\": true/false, \"clarification_compliant\": true/false, \"rewrite_instruction\": \"...\"}\n    "}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-24T06:41:08.481+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_53fff7d9-27ae-483e-9a4c-e2fd61d1a6a5", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    GROUNDEDNESS v2.0 — EVIDENCE AUDIT\n    You are an evidence-groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank assistant.\n\n    Permitted Evidence (Task-Level Approved Evidence, Pending Service Requests, and Unavailable Service Requests — the only factual sources for answers and answer UI):\n    {\"approved_by_task\": [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"resolved_subquery\": \"Report a lost credit card\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_33f045af\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card has been compromised due to physical damage. What steps should I take to obtain a new one from Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To acquire a replacement card, follow these straightforward steps: \\n    * Access your Horizon App account \\n    * Navigate to the 'Card Management' section \\n    * Choose the 'Replace Current Card' option \\n    * Indicate that your card is damaged to complete the request\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7883a8c2\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \\\"Freeze Card.\\\"\\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \\\"Freeze Card\\\" followed by \\\"Order Replacement.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\\n- For additional assistance, select \\\"Contact Us\\\" from the app menu.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_83fb94a7\", \"content\": \"Question: If I request a lost‑card replacement for my current Horizon Link credit/debit card, will the existing physical card still accumulate Linkpoints while I wait for the new one?\\n\\nAnswer: - No. After you select the lost‑card replacement option, the original Horizon Link card stops earning Linkpoints. You will only be able to collect points with the replacement NTUC Link credit/debit card once it arrives, or through the FairPrice app by entering the new NTUC Link card details that appear in your Horizon App during the interim.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_98eb6af4\", \"content\": \"Question: I'm currently using my Horizon Link Credit/Debit Card, but my Horizon App displays the NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card. How can I obtain a physical version of the NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card?\\n\\nAnswer: To receive a physical NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card, you'll need to initiate a lost card replacement process through the Horizon App. It's essential to choose the correct replacement option, as selecting 'damaged card' will not yield the desired outcome. Please be aware that replacing your card will result in changes to your card details, including the card number, CVV, and expiry date. Consequently, you will need to update your card information for any existing online credit card arrangements, such as card-on-file and recurring payments, to ensure uninterrupted service.\"}]}], \"pending_service_requests\": [{\"special_id\": \"GH80Z9tYIVRjoXXuLfkxnQM12yuq49B7\", \"service_request_id\": \"profile-address-update\", \"description\": \"Submit a new postal address for the customer's profile.\"}], \"unavailable_service_requests\": []}\n\n    Customer-Facing Content:\n    \n        Original Customer Message (courtesy-context onl