 \"listIntro\": \"\", \"extendedText\": \"\"}, {\"type\": \"text\", \"contextText\": \"\", \"text\": \"To move forward, please complete the form below: Submit a new postal address for the customer's profile.\", \"items\": [], \"options\": [], \"progressTitle\": \"\", \"stepDetails\": [], \"currentStep\": null, \"totalSteps\": null, \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"extendedText\": \"\"}]}\"\n    \n\n    TASK: Assess CONDUCT & COMPLIANCE ONLY. Do not assess whether facts are\n    supported by evidence — a separate auditor handles that.\n\n\n    Output JSON only:\n    {\"conduct_compliant\": true/false, \"reason\": \"...\", \"conduct_violations\": [{\"rule\": \"bank_conduct\" | \"regulation\", \"violation\": \"...\", \"unsupported_content\": [\"verbatim phrase\"]}], \"answer_compliant\": true/false, \"clarification_compliant\": true/false, \"rewrite_instruction\": \"...\"}\n    "}
{"timestamp": "2026-08-24T07:18:45.583+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_76e303a9-1ae3-4a25-8d1a-947d608f8c81", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    GROUNDEDNESS v2.0 — EVIDENCE AUDIT\n    You are an evidence-groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank assistant.\n\n    Permitted Evidence (Task-Level Approved Evidence, Pending Service Requests, and Unavailable Service Requests — the only factual sources for answers and answer UI):\n    {\"approved_by_task\": [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"resolved_subquery\": \"I lost my credit card and need to know the procedure for reporting it.\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7883a8c2\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \\\"Freeze Card.\\\"\\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \\\"Freeze Card\\\" followed by \\\"Order Replacement.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\\n- For additional assistance, select \\\"Contact Us\\\" from the app menu.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"resolved_subquery\": \"I want to change my registered address.\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_24568045\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for changing my personal details—address, phone number, or email—within the Horizon ecosystem?\\n\\nAnswer: - Updating your personal information can now be done directly through the Horizon App.\\n{{faq_24568045_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n{{faq_24568045_002}}. Tap the Profile icon located at the upper‑right corner.\\n{{faq_24568045_003}}. Within Profile, navigate to Settings ► Personal Details.\\n{{faq_24568045_004}}. Choose the field you wish to modify (address, phone number, or email).\\n{{faq_24568045_005}}. For phone number or email changes, enter the one‑time password (OTP) sent to you.\\n{{faq_24568045_006}}. Provide your Horizon Key for additional verification before the update is applied.\\n{{faq_24568045_007}}. After you submit, the change will be processed within {{faq_24568045_008}} hours for phone numbers and email addresses, while address updates take effect instantly.\"}]}], \"pending_service_requests\": [{\"special_id\": \"OfrxCWNhka5QVoRNcOAEdEENd-Y2eJox\", \"service_request_id\": \"profile-address-update\", \"description\": \"Submit a new postal address for the customer's profile.\"}], \"unavailable_service_requests\": []}\n\n    Customer-Facing Content:\n    \n        Original Customer Message (courtesy-context only; never a source for a\n        banking fact, instruction, product capability, policy, or outcome):\n        \"i lost my credit card, what should i do, also i want to change my address too\"\n\n        Optional Internal Response-Element Provenance (not customer-facing):\n        [{\"block_id\": \"element_1\", \"source_task_ids\": [\"task_2\"]}, {\"block_id\": \"element_fallback_task_1\", \"source_task_ids\": [\"task_1\"]}]\n\n        Intent Clarification Inputs (the only source for intent clarification):\n        []\n\n        Terminal Unresolved Task Markers (topic/status only; never evidence):\n        []\n\n        Decline Inputs (the only source for a declined-topic explanation):\n        []\n\n        Customer-Facing Answer:\n        \"Please complete the form below to submit a new postal address for your profile.\n\nIf you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it or request a replacement through the Horizon App by signing in, opening the card dashboard, choosing \"View & Manage Card,\" and tapping \"Freeze Card\" followed by \"Order Replacement.\"\n\nSorry, I don't have a complete answer for the part about I lost my credit card and need to know the procedure for reporting it. right now.\n\nTo move forward, please complete the form below: Submit a new postal address for the customer's profile.\"\n\n        Customer-Facing Clarification:\n        \"\"\n\n        Complete Customer-Facing UI Payload:\n        \"{\"uiType\": \"blocks\", \"options\": [], \"stepDetails\": [], \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"items\": [], \"extendedText\": \"\", \"listClarificationText\": \"\", \"responseBlocks\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"contextText\": \"\", \"text\": \"Please complete the form below to submit a new postal address for your profile.\\n\\nIf you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it or request a replacement through the Horizon App by signing in, opening the card dashboard, choosing \\\"View & Manage Card,\\\" and tapping \\\"Freeze Card\\\" followed by \\\"Order Replacement.\\\"\", \"items\": [], \"options\": [], \"progressTitle\": \"\", \"stepDetails\": [], \"currentStep\": null, \"totalSteps\": null, \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"extendedText\": \"\"}, {\"type\": \"text\", \"contextText\": \"\", \"text\": \"Sorry, I don't have a complete answer for the part about I lost my credit card and need to know the procedure for reporting it. right now.\", \"items\": [], \"options\": [], \"progressTitle\": \"\", \"stepDetails\": [], \"currentStep\": null, \"totalSteps\": null, \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"extendedText\": \"\"}, {\"type\": \"text\", \"contextText\": \"\", \"text\": \"To move forward, please complete the form below: Submit a new postal address for the customer's profile.\", \"items\": [], \"options\": [], \"progressTitle\": \"\", \"stepDetails\": [], \"currentStep\": null, \"totalSteps\": null, \"listTitle\": \"\", \"listIntro\": \"\", \"extendedText\": \"\"}]}\"\n        \n\n    \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n\n    TASK: Assess EVIDENCE GROUNDEDNESS ONLY. Do not assess conduct, tone,\n    regulatory compliance, or completeness — a separate auditor handles those.\n    Every factual claim, instruction, figure, or suggestion in the Customer-Facing\n    Content must be directly supported by the Permitted Evidence above; nothing\n    outside it may be used as a factual source.\n\n    \n        ANSWER AUDIT: assess the customer's natural answer as one coherent\n        response. Do NOT require it to be written in separate factual and\n        inferential sections. Instead, distinguish the following two internal\n        checks while reading the same natural answer and answer UI.\n\n        1. Direct Factual Grounding (Evidence Check)\n        - Every explicit factual assertion, parameter, eligibility rule,\n          product capability, policy condition, limit, date, amount,\n          placeholder, instruction, option, progress step, list item,\n          extended-text statement, and answer response-block field must be\n          directly supported by the Permitted Evidence (Task-Level Approved\n          Evidence) above.\n        - Assess the answer and answer UI as one coherent customer response\n          against the aggregate Task-Level Approved Evidence. The response does\n          not need a visible section, element, or title for each task.\n        - When an optional response element is mapped to source_task_ids, its\n          factual content may use the union of approved evidence for those\n          tasks. An unmapped element may use any Task-Level Approved Evidence.\n        2. Inferential Grounding (Bridge Check)\n        - Natural conclusions that connect approved facts to the resolved\n          sub-query are allowed when they are a reasonable, bounded logical\n          implication of the approved evidence. Do not require verbatim FAQ\n          wording for such a conclusion.\n        - Reject a bridge only when it adds an unstated premise, actor,\n          policy, procedure, reason, certainty, exception, or consequence; or\n          when the conclusion is not entailed by the approved evidence.\n        - Example: evidence that explicitly sets a maximum coverage cap can\n          support the bounded conclusion that coverage cannot be increased\n          above that cap. It does NOT support attributing control of the cap\n          to a particular bank, regulator, or process unless that attribution\n          is explicit in the evidence.\n\n        Courtesy Context Rule (applies to the answer, clarification, and UI):\n        - First isolate any brief conversational courtesy acknowledgement,\n          greeting, thanks, apology, or response to the customer's stated\n          feeling or preference. It is grounded when it faithfully responds to\n          the Original Customer Message and introduces no banking fact,\n          procedure, product/service capability, policy, eligibility,\n          commitment, recommendation, availability conclusion, or next action.\n          Do not fail such a courtesy sentence merely because it is absent from\n          Task-Level Approved Evidence.\n        - Assess every remaining financial statement and UI field only against\n          Task-Level Approved Evidence. The Original Customer Message can\n          never support, soften, or justify a financial claim.\n\n        Clarification Rules:\n        - For an intent clarification, every named unresolved term must come\n          only from Intent Clarification Inputs. Do not infer a product, policy,\n          or banking fact.\n        - For a terminal unresolved task, a neutral statement that available\n          information does not resolve its named request is grounded. It must\n          not state, suggest, or imply a banking fact, procedure, product\n          alternative, policy, or next action unless supported by Task-Level\n          Approved Evidence.\n        - A generic apology and a general request for clarification are grounded.\n        - A clarification following an answer must identify its unresolved term\n          instead of using an ambiguous reference such as \"that\" or \"it\".\n        - For a decline explanation, only the exact subquery named in Decline\n          Inputs may be referenced; it must not assert a specific Horizon\n          product, policy, fee, or commitment as the reason, and must never\n          provide the declined advice, action, or information itself. Every\n          entry in Decline Inputs must be explicitly named somewhere in the\n          clarification, not silently omitted — treat a missing entry as\n          equivalent to an unidentified reference for clarification_connected.\n\n        \n    Audit-Feedback Rules:\n    - grounding